{"id":269053990183040,"type":"artist","name":"Heldon","artist":null,"year":1974,"weight":21,"info":{"tags":["Progressive rock","electronic","Avant-Garde","psychedelic","french"],"country":"FR","begin":"1974","end":"1979","kind":"Group","similar":["Richard Pinhas","A.R. & Machines","Magma","Faust","Ash Ra Tempel","Amon Düül II","Henry Cow","Eskaton","Cluster","Samla Mammas Manna"],"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/a288a2147c490e38d7f8b3fd8075fd90/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg","bio":"Led by guitarist Richard Pinhas, the French group Heldon released seven groundbreaking albums, melding electronic and rock forms, from 1974 to 1978. Pinhas also recorded six albums under his own name. \n\nPinhas was heavily influenced by Robert Fripp; this shows in his guitar playing, and in the titles of several of his compositions. While early LPs sometimes evoked the sound of Fripp and Eno, Heldon evolved in its own direction with heavy use of Mellotrons and Moog synthesizers and a Fripp influenced guitar tonality."},"works":[{"id":248059478717119,"type":"album","name":"Electronique Guerilla","artist":"Heldon","year":1974,"weight":13,"yt":"XS0WuJrp_4I","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":65232636722211,"name":"Scaruffi 1970s","rank":321,"scaruffi":7.0},{"id":106284046011718,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — Progressive Electronic","rank":160,"scaruffi":7.0}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":143989691392276,"type":"album","name":"Allez Téia","artist":"Heldon","year":1975,"weight":3,"yt":"Jz5RoY6A96s","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":106284046011718,"name":"RYM Top — Electronic — Progressive Electronic","rank":90,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":266119137844663,"type":"album","name":"It's Always Rock And Roll","artist":"Heldon","year":1975,"weight":15,"yt":"oZmYvCFIOKQ","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruff